Handling errors in this SDK should largely match your expectations. All operations return a response object or throw an exception.

By default, an API error will raise a `{{templateDefaultError true}}` exception, which has the following properties:

| Property      | Type                  | Description           |
|---------------|-----------------------|-----------------------|
| `Message`     | *string*              | The error message     |
{{- if eq getResponseFormat "envelope-http" }}
| `Request`     | *HttpRequestMessage*  | The HTTP request      |
| `Response`    | *HttpResponseMessage* | The HTTP response     |
{{- else}}
| `StatusCode`  | *int*                 | The raw HTTP response |
| `RawResponse` | *HttpResponseMessage* | The raw HTTP response |
| `Body`        | *string*              | The response content  |
{{- end}}

When custom error responses are specified for an operation, the SDK may also throw their associated exception. You can refer to respective *Errors* tables in SDK docs for more details on possible exception types for each operation. For example, the `{{sanitizeMethodName .Local.UsageContext.Operation}}Async` method throws the following exceptions:

{{templateErrorsTable .Local.UsageContext.Operation}}

